## SQ-RB-21b | Copper Pot, 3 meals' inputs and 1 bowl in slot 5: no bowl lost (pure bowl-food recipe)
# r1103 p2: the probe's last pick (rusticdelight:cooking/fried_chicken) also leaves a glass bottle (cooking oil); with
# a bowl in slot 5 that pot never started (CopperPotBlockEntity.leftoversFit: bowl and bottle both need slot 7), judged
# FAIL. This rerun uses kangaroo pasta (tomato sauce leaves a bowl, nothing else), NBT from the p2 potnbt3 line.
> kill @e[type=minecraft:item]
> setblock {S5H1+50} {S5H2} {S5H3+24} minecraft:campfire[lit=true]
> setblock {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+24} miners_delight:copper_pot
> data merge block {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+24} {Inventory:{Size:8,Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"alexsdelight:cooked_kangaroo_shank",Count:3b},{Slot:1b,id:"farmersdelight:raw_pasta",Count:3b},{Slot:2b,id:"farmersdelight:tomato_sauce",Count:3b},{Slot:5b,id:"minecraft:bowl",Count:1b}]}}
pace 1
repeat 8
sleep 6
> data get block {S5H1+50} {S5H2+1} {S5H3+24}
end
pace 2
> zcount {S5H1+48} {S5H2} {S5H3+22} {S5H1+52} {S5H2+3} {S5H3+26}
waitlog \[zcount\] entities 30
expect Slot: 6, id: "alexsdelight:kangaroo_pasta", Count: 3b
reject \[zcount\] entities .*item:minecraft:bowl
look over the readings CookTimeTotal is above 0 (the pot runs); slot 5 never holds more bowls than meals still waiting, extra bowls in slot 7; at the end bowls before (1 + 3 recycled) = slot 5 + slot 7 + plated meals

## SQ-DRK-04 | spout fills a bottle from Kiwi Tea (diagnostic: recipe presence)
# r1103 p2: every spout line read "needs -1 mB, gives nothing" (no filling recipe matched) while the drain worked;
# NCH createBottle makes the filling and emptying pair together. List both recipes and retry the spout.
> zq recipes kiwi_tea
> zq recipes lychee_juice
> zq bytype create:filling
> s5 spout creativeengineering:kiwi_tea 250 minecraft:glass_bottle
> s5 spout minecraft:water 250 minecraft:glass_bottle
expect \[zq\] \S*filling\S*kiwi_tea\S* ->
expect \[s5\] spout creativeengineering:kiwi_tea 250 mB into minecraft:glass_bottle: can true, needs 250 mB, gives creativeengineering:kiwi_tea x1
look the water spout line is the probe control (vanilla potion fill); if it also reads -1, the probe is wrong, not the pack

